  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#OperatingModel">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Operating Model</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">Modele Operationnel</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The way a capability is operationally delivered within an org unit.
This is NOT a single enterprise-wide choice but a per-capability
per-domain determination that emerges from reality.

Key values (from conversation 2026-02-09):
  - Centralized: CDO office / central team delivers for this domain
  - Federated: Domain operates its own instance of this capability
  - Shared: Central platform consumed by domain (shared service)
  - Absent: No coverage — structural gap
  - Shadow: Unofficial/unrecognized implementation (pre-formalization)
  - Emerging: Capability developing organically, not yet formalized
  - Contested: Multiple teams claim ownership, divergent approaches</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
