  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#Dimension">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#DOMElement" />
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dimension</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">Dimension</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">One of the four orthogonal dimensions (People, Process, Systems, Data) that apply to every capability. Phase 2 will fully specify.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">One of the four orthogonal dimensions through which every DOM capability
is analyzed. A capability reaches maturity only when all four dimensions
are aligned. Investing in tools (Systems) without skills (People) or
processes (Process) is the primary cause of data initiative failure.
(DOM Chapter 2.2)</rdfs:comment>
