  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#CapabilityAssignment">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Capability Assignment</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">Affectation de Capability</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The CORE of the Organizational Mapper. Links a specific L3 capability
to a specific organizational unit, capturing:
  - WHO carries it (which org unit)
  - HOW it is carried (operating model)
  - HOW WELL (maturity scores per dimension)
  - WHETHER it's the observed reality or the strategic target
  - WHEN this was assessed (temporal tracking)

This is what transforms 'Data Quality is at 3/5' into 'Data Quality
is at 4/5 in Finance, 1/5 in the acquired subsidiary, and absent in
the Innovation department.'

Key insight: the operating model is per-capability per-domain, NOT
a single enterprise-wide choice. Finance may run Data Quality in
federated mode while Supply Chain relies on centralized delivery.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#RUN_L2.2_L3.4_EnterpriseSearchInformationRetrieval">
