  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#KPI">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Key Performance Indicator</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">Indicateur de Performance Cle</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A KPI from the DOM's three-tier hierarchy (274 KPIs). Phase 5 will fully specify.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A KPI from the DOM's three-tier hierarchy (259 KPIs per book,
274 per extended toolkit). Each KPI has a tier, BSC perspective,
indicator type, target, frequency, and cascading relationships.</rdfs:comment>
    <dom:phaseHook>Phase 5 - Framework Integration &amp; KPIs</dom:phaseHook>
    <dom:bookChapter>Chapter 5 - KPI Framework &amp; Executive Scorecard</dom:bookChapter>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#RACIAssignment">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" />
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">RACI Assignment</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">Affectation RACI</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Links a Stakeholder type to an L3 capability with a RACI role.
This is the atomic cell of a RACI matrix.

Generated from Section 9 (Stakeholders) → primary R/A assignments,
Section 8 (Input Suppliers) → C assignments,
Section 13 (Outcomes Consumers) → I assignments.

Can be further scoped to an OrganizationalUnit (Phase 3) to produce
per-domain RACI matrices for federated/hybrid models.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
