  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.1_L3.1_S06">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionContent"/>
    <dom:belongsToSpecification rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.1_L3.1"/>
    <dom:forSection rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#Section_06_DataEconomics"/>
    <dom:textContent>This capability carries the highest economic leverage in the DOM — a well-constructed data strategy directs hundreds of millions in platform, talent, and programme investment toward value-generating activities. The cost of strategy failure routinely exceeds strategy development costs by two to three orders of magnitude. ROI materialises through avoided waste, accelerated business case approval cycles, and sustained executive funding.</dom:textContent>
  </rdf:Description>
