  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.1_L3.2_S06">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionContent"/>
    <dom:belongsToSpecification rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.1_L3.2"/>
    <dom:forSection rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#Section_06_DataEconomics"/>
    <dom:textContent>This capability is itself a value multiplier — by directing capital toward high-return data programmes and away from low-value initiatives, it generates financial leverage that compounds across the portfolio. Organisations with mature data investment frameworks report 30-50% improvement in data programme ROI through better prioritisation alone. The framework also unlocks access to larger capital allocations by satisfying CFO-level financial governance requirements.</dom:textContent>
  </rdf:Description>
