  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.1_S06">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionContent"/>
    <dom:belongsToSpecification rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.1"/>
    <dom:forSection rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#Section_06_DataEconomics"/>
    <dom:textContent>Effective governance frameworks reduce regulatory risk premiums embedded in data programme budgets — organisations with mature governance spend 20-35% less on compliance remediation activities. The governance framework also acts as an investment efficiency mechanism: decisions made through proper governance channels have materially lower reversal and rework rates, typically reducing programme cost overruns by 15-25%.</dom:textContent>
  </rdf:Description>
