  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.2_S06">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionContent"/>
    <dom:belongsToSpecification rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.2"/>
    <dom:forSection rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#Section_06_DataEconomics"/>
    <dom:textContent>Compliance is asymmetrically costly — investment in proactive compliance is a fraction of the cost of reactive enforcement response. GDPR investigation costs typically run 5-15x the cost of the compliance programme that would have prevented them. Strong compliance posture is increasingly a commercial prerequisite — enterprise customers require evidence of data compliance in vendor due diligence.</dom:textContent>
  </rdf:Description>
