  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.3_S01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionContent"/>
    <dom:belongsToSpecification rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.3"/>
    <dom:forSection rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#Section_01_Definition"/>
    <dom:textContent>Establishes and operates the data ownership and stewardship model assigning accountable custodians to every significant data domain, dataset, and data product. Ensures data assets have named humans responsible for their quality, fitness for purpose, and appropriate use — eliminating the 'nobody owns it' failure mode.</dom:textContent>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.3_S02">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionContent"/>
    <dom:belongsToSpecification rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.3"/>
    <dom:forSection rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#Section_02_BusinessContext"/>
    <dom:textContent>Unowned data degrades predictably and rapidly. Without named owners and stewards, data quality issues propagate without triggering remediation, definitions drift between business units creating analytical inconsistency, and sensitive data is misused without accountability. Data ownership is the single most effective intervention for sustained data quality improvement.</dom:textContent>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.3_S03_I1">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionItem"/>
    <dom:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</dom:itemOrder>
    <dom:itemText>Data Ownership Model — Framework defining Data Owner and Data Steward roles, responsibilities, authority, and organisational positioning</dom:itemText>
    <dom:relatedDimension>People</dom:relatedDimension>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.3_S03_I2">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionItem"/>
    <dom:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</dom:itemOrder>
    <dom:itemText>Domain Ownership Assignment — Process for identifying, nominating, and formalising data owners across all significant data domains</dom:itemText>
    <dom:relatedDimension>People</dom:relatedDimension>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.3_S03_I3">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionItem"/>
    <dom:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</dom:itemOrder>
    <dom:itemText>Stewardship Network — Operational community of data stewards working within domains under data owner direction</dom:itemText>
    <dom:relatedDimension>People</dom:relatedDimension>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.3_S03_I4">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionItem"/>
    <dom:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</dom:itemOrder>
    <dom:itemText>Ownership Lifecycle Management — Processes for onboarding new data assets with owners and transitioning ownership at personnel changes</dom:itemText>
    <dom:relatedDimension>Process</dom:relatedDimension>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.3_S03_I5">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionItem"/>
    <dom:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</dom:itemOrder>
    <dom:itemText>Owner Accountability Mechanisms — Performance expectations, KPIs, and accountability structures making ownership substantive rather than ceremonial</dom:itemText>
    <dom:relatedDimension>Process</dom:relatedDimension>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.2_L3.3_S03">
