  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.2_S01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionContent"/>
    <dom:belongsToSpecification rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.2"/>
    <dom:forSection rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#Section_01_Definition"/>
    <dom:textContent>Establishes and enforces the non-negotiable architectural principles and security-by-design standards governing all data platform and pipeline design decisions. These principles are the standing constraints within which BUILD constructs and MANAGE operates — encoding organisational risk appetite, regulatory requirements, and architectural good practices into mandatory design rules.</dom:textContent>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.2_S02">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionContent"/>
    <dom:belongsToSpecification rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.2"/>
    <dom:forSection rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#Section_02_BusinessContext"/>
    <dom:textContent>Without architectural principles enforced at design time, security and compliance requirements are retrofitted at enormous cost — post-deployment remediation of architectural security gaps costs 10-100x more than design-time prevention. Unprincipled architectures accumulate structural debt that eventually requires costly platform rebuilds. Principles create predictability: development teams with clear constraints make faster, better decisions than those improvising architecture under delivery pressure.</dom:textContent>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.2_S03_I1">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionItem"/>
    <dom:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</dom:itemOrder>
    <dom:itemText>Data Architecture Principles Library — Documented, ratified principles covering data sovereignty, minimisation, quality, interoperability, and resilience</dom:itemText>
    <dom:relatedDimension>Data</dom:relatedDimension>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.2_S03_I2">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionItem"/>
    <dom:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</dom:itemOrder>
    <dom:itemText>Security-by-Design Standards — Mandatory security patterns for data at rest, in transit, and in use — embedded as design requirements rather than post-build additions</dom:itemText>
    <dom:relatedDimension>Systems</dom:relatedDimension>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.2_S03_I3">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionItem"/>
    <dom:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</dom:itemOrder>
    <dom:itemText>Privacy-by-Design Integration — Architectural privacy requirements ensuring personal data minimisation, purpose limitation, and consent propagation by design</dom:itemText>
    <dom:relatedDimension>Process</dom:relatedDimension>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.2_S03_I4">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionItem"/>
    <dom:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</dom:itemOrder>
    <dom:itemText>Principles Enforcement Mechanism — Architecture review gates, automated compliance checks, and exception management for principle deviations</dom:itemText>
    <dom:relatedDimension>Process</dom:relatedDimension>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.2_S03_I5">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionItem"/>
    <dom:itemOrder rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</dom:itemOrder>
    <dom:itemText>Principles Evolution — Structured process for updating principles as technology, regulation, and organisational context evolve</dom:itemText>
    <dom:relatedDimension>Process</dom:relatedDimension>
  </rdf:Description>
