  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.2_S06">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionContent"/>
    <dom:belongsToSpecification rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.2"/>
    <dom:forSection rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#Section_06_DataEconomics"/>
    <dom:textContent>Architecture principles represent the highest-leverage governance investment per unit of effort — a well-designed principle, once embedded in development standards, generates compliance dividends across every subsequent data build without incremental cost. Security-by-design specifically prevents the most expensive class of data incidents: those caused by architectural vulnerabilities. Prevention costs estimated at 1-5% of the remediation cost of a material data breach attributable to architectural weakness.</dom:textContent>
  </rdf:Description>
