  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.3_S06">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SectionContent"/>
    <dom:belongsToSpecification rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#SPEC_GOVERN_L2.3_L3.3"/>
    <dom:forSection rdf:resource="http://strategic-advisory.com/ontology/dom/2.0#Section_06_DataEconomics"/>
    <dom:textContent>Technology lifecycle management prevents the most insidious form of data infrastructure cost: stranded investment in platforms that could not be retired cleanly because they were adopted without lifecycle management. Reference architectures reduce per-project architecture design cost by 30-50% by providing pre-validated patterns. Technology consolidation enabled by Radar discipline typically reduces data tool licensing cost by 20-30%.</dom:textContent>
  </rdf:Description>
